+## Verification run
+
+- Ran in a review-owned detached worktree at 2dfa656 (.worktrees/review-c8-b9c53a9d, target reflinked from the caller's warm build): `toolbox run -c hg-build cargo test --lib -- store::history inspect::scope store::instruction_source writer::recovery` gave 22 passed, 0 failed. These were all 8 `store::history` tests and all 14 `inspect::scope` tests, including `pick_live_only_keeps_retired_error`, `pick_retired_allowed_rule` and `instructions_show_still_rejects_retired_name`.
+- `toolbox run -c hg-build cargo test --lib -- writer:: instructions` gave 104 passed, 0 failed. This covers the recovery path that now calls the shared `parse_trailers`.
+- The leak check (`/tmp/hg-*` cwd count) printed 0 afterwards. The review worktree and its target/ were removed.
+
+## What the cluster delivers
+
+- `store::history::HistoryWalker` is the spec's HistoryWalker. It walks newest-first along the first parent from a given `CommitId`, never from HEAD it resolves itself, so the one-pinned-HEAD rule of §2.1 holds. It reads the `Graph-Op`/`Graph-Action` trailers through one `parse_trailers`, the `OperationRecord` and `ActionRecord` from each commit's own tree, and the changed paths against the first parent (every file for a root commit). It applies a scan cap with a `ScanReport {scanned, max_scan, stopped_early}`, a one-pass `last_touches`, and `action_at_head` for the undone column, which is read at the pinned HEAD and not at the commit (§2.4).
+- `stopped_early` semantics match §2.4: true only when the cap was reached with older commits left. A cap equal to the history length is not an early stop, and a callback `Break` is not one either. All three cases are tested.
+- Malformed records match §2.1 and the HistoryWalker Errors paragraph. A trailer whose record does not parse, or is missing from the commit's diff, gives `operation`/`action` = None plus `malformed` naming it, and the walk continues. The init commit comes through as an unattributed `Change`.
+- The trailer parser was extracted, not duplicated: `writer::recovery::trailers_since` now calls `store::history::parse_trailers`. The parser's behavior is identical to the inline loop it replaces: last occurrence wins, and an unparsable value becomes None.
+- Record lookup in an undo commit is correct. The undo writes two action records (the new undo action, plus the original's `undone_by`, `src/undo/compensate.rs:254-276`). `read_record` picks the file whose stem equals the trailer's id, so it gets the undo action and not the original.
+- `instruction_source::pick` gains `PickMode`. Under `LiveOnly` the match arms reduce to the old ones: no matches gives UnknownTarget, retired-only gives Retired, several live gives Ambiguous. `resolve_scope` delegates with `LiveOnly`, so `instructions show` resolution and its `Retired` error are unchanged, as the Unchanged-behavior list requires. Under `RetiredAllowed` the rule is the Scope rule from Key abstractions. One live match wins. Several live matches are ambiguous. With no live match, one retired match resolves and several are ambiguous, and the error lists every id. An id resolves whatever its lifecycle, and `list_teamspaces`/`all_seats` include `archive/`. The error wording is shared through `ambiguous()`.
+
