+## Untested scope
+- No HistoryWalker test with a merge commit on `main` to pin first-parent behavior (the writer never makes merge commits, so this is latent).
+- No test of a trailer whose record is absent from the commit's diff; only unparsable records are covered (`malformed_records_flagged`).
+- No test of record selection in an undo-shaped commit that changes two action records (`action_at_head_reads_undone` commits the undo without trailers).
+- No test that pins the walk cost independent of history length (the `Sort::TOPOLOGICAL` full-chain preparation).
+
+## Deferred OK
+- `Sort::TOPOLOGICAL` in `HistoryWalker::commits` makes revwalk preparation O(full history) despite the scan cap (verified in libgit2 1.9.7 revwalk.c); a performance issue only, and `Sort::NONE` with first-parent gives the same order on the writer's linear history.
+- `last_touches` scans to the cap when given duplicate input paths; a performance issue only.
+- `last_touches` cannot tell "never touched" from "beyond the cap" (no ScanReport); §2.3 does not require it for `path last touched`.
+- `store::history` depends on `undo::candidates::read_action` (store importing undo); a cosmetic layering point.
